GEOS thirdPartyLibs 9b55672f6f8a73d02fd632396eb0410e58c9b120 (TPL tag 361-1070) -- hdf5 step: use the superbuild's generator and build/install commands

Class: build-system compatibility fix (no source/algorithm change).
Problem: every CMake-based ExternalProject step passes
`CMAKE_GENERATOR ${TPL_GENERATOR}` and uses ${TPL_BUILD_COMMAND}/${TPL_INSTALL_COMMAND}
(make / ninja, selected by ENABLE_NINJA, CMakeLists.txt lines 86-96) -- except
hdf5, which passes no generator and hardcodes `make -j ${NUM_PROC}` / `make install`.
When the superbuild itself is generated with Ninja (`scripts/config-build.py -n`,
upstream's documented option) the hdf5 sub-build inherits the Ninja generator
from the parent and its hardcoded make step fails with "make: *** No targets
specified and no makefile found". Fix: give the hdf5 step the same generator and
build/install commands as all other steps. Impact: none on the built HDF5 1.12.1
(same configure options; only the generator/driver of its own build). Verified:
TPL superbuild proceeds past hdf5 under a Ninja-generated superbuild. Applied by
level3/geos/build.sh (git apply, idempotent); recorded in the profile fingerprint.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -259,8 +259,9 @@
                      URL_HASH SHA256=${HDF5_URL_HASH}
                      PREFIX ${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}/hdf5
                      INSTALL_DIR ${HDF5_DIR}
-                     BUILD_COMMAND make -j ${NUM_PROC}
-                     INSTALL_COMMAND make install
+                     BUILD_COMMAND ${TPL_BUILD_COMMAND}
+                     INSTALL_COMMAND ${TPL_INSTALL_COMMAND}
+                     CMAKE_GENERATOR ${TPL_GENERATOR}
                      CMAKE_ARGS -D CMAKE_C_COMPILER:STRING=${HDF5_C_COMPILER}
                                 -D CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER:STRING=${HDF5_CXX_COMPILER}
                                 -D CMAKE_C_FLAGS:STRING=${C_FLAGS_NO_WARNINGS}
